  <div class="article-header">
    <h1>Standish Medical Cannabis Guide</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Lakewood Cannabis, patient access, and what Standish's local ordinance actually allows</p>
  </div>

  <section class="fact-box">
    <h2>Standish cannabis access at a glance</h2>
    <table aria-label="Standish cannabis access facts">
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">In-town store</th><td>Lakewood Cannabis</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Program</th><td>Maine medical cannabis</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Location</th><td>234 Northeast Road, Unit 15, Standish, ME 04084</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Adult-use retail</th><td>Expressly prohibited by Standish Chapter 220</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Medical use</th><td>Chapter 220 says it is not intended to prohibit lawful conduct under Maine's medical-use law</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <Callout title="Standish is medical—not an adult-use opt-in market" type="warning">
    Standish's current code expressly prohibits adult-use retail stores, products manufacturing facilities, testing facilities, and social clubs. The same ordinance preserves lawful medical-use activity. Do not treat the presence of a medical dispensary as proof that the town has opted in to adult-use retail.
  </Callout>

  <section>
    <h2>Lakewood Cannabis in Standish</h2>
    <p><strong>Lakewood Cannabis</strong> identifies its Standish store as a medical cannabis provider at <strong>234 Northeast Road, Unit 15</strong>. Its current operator page lists the telephone number <strong>(207) 648-4414</strong> and publishes store hours of Sunday through Wednesday, 10 a.m.–7 p.m., and Thursday through Saturday, 8 a.m.–8 p.m.</p>
    <p>Because hours and day-to-day availability can change, confirm directly with the operator before traveling. See the <a href="https://lakewood-cannabis.com/standish-store/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lakewood Cannabis Standish store page</a> for the current listing.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Standish Chapter 220 says</h2>
    <p>The <a href="https://ecode360.com/32867669" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Town of Standish Code, Chapter 220</a>, separates adult-use establishments from medical cannabis activity:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Section 220-3(A)</strong> expressly prohibits adult-use retail stores, products manufacturing facilities, testing facilities, and social clubs.</li>
      <li><strong>Section 220-3(B)</strong> bars a business from engaging in adult-use retail sales covered by the ordinance.</li>
      <li><strong>Section 220-3(C)</strong> says the chapter is not intended to prohibit lawful use, possession, or conduct under the Maine Medical Use of Cannabis Act.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This distinction explains why Standish can have a medical dispensary while prohibiting the adult-use categories named in its local ordinance.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>State records and operator status</h2>
    <p>OCP's medical-establishment file dated June 1, 2026 identifies active registration DSP184 in Standish for Inhale Zen, LLC, doing business as “Lakewood Cananbis” in the state file. The operator's current site also labels its state licenses as medical retail. Together, the current regulator file and operator page support the medical classification; they do not establish adult-use authorization.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/sites/maine.gov.dafs.ocp/files/inline-files/Maine_Medical_Use_Establishments_2026_06_01.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OCP medical-use establishment file — June 1, 2026</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://lakewood-cannabis.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lakewood Cannabis operator website</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Before visiting</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirm that the store is open and that the current menu fits your needs.</li>
      <li>Bring the identification and medical credentials required for a Maine medical cannabis purchase.</li>
      <li>If you are visiting Maine, review OCP's current visiting-patient rules before relying on an out-of-state credential.</li>
      <li>Do not assume that statewide adult-use legality means an adult-use storefront is locally authorized in Standish.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>OCP explains the two separate programs in its <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/resources/faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">consumer and medical-use FAQ</a>.</p>
  </section>

